meta {
  name: Auto routing
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/chat/completions
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{apiKey}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "model": "auto",
    "messages": [
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "What is the capital of France?"
      }
    ],
    "temperature": 0.0
  }
}

docs {
  Lets the configured routing policy pick the model.

  With GATEWAY_ROUTING_POLICY=static (default) "auto" serves the high-quality
  tier with the budget fallback. With GATEWAY_ROUTING_POLICY=autopilot the
  llm-cost-autopilot sidecar classifies the prompt and the gateway maps its
  tier to a model; if autopilot is slow or down, the static policy is used.

  Response headers:
  - `X-Gateway-Model-Used`      the model that served the request
  - `X-Gateway-Routing-Reason`  why, e.g. autopilot_simple_stage_1_embedding
}
